tation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the exit-code contract for the migrated observables: note that reconcile-check is exit-0-always (no discrepancy-driven exit) and state, per owner, whether discrepancies/orphans now influence the owner's exit (preview/sync 0/1/2, fsck 0/1/2 findings) or whether exit-0-always is the parity target to preserve.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["__main__.py reconcile-check path returns 0 on success and 1 only on exception (lines 267-277) — discrepancies never alter the exit code","_finish_disposition maps preview/sync to disposition.canonical_exit (0/1/2); bridge_fsck.main docstring: 'Returns 0 clean, 1 findings, or 2 operational failure'","Plan asks to 'preserve the preserved diagnostics, formatting, exits' without reconciling the exit-0-always source contract against the 0/1/2 target contracts"],"finding":"The plan requires preserving 'exits' and 'field/format/exit parity', but reconcile-check's actual CLI contract returns exit 0 unconditionally (discrepancies/orphans do NOT change the exit code; only an exception -> 1), whereas the named owners have divergent exit semantics (bridge preview/sync 0/1/2 by pass disposition; bridge fsck 0/1/2 clean/findings/failure). Splitting observables across owners with heterogeneous exit contracts makes 'exit parity' under-specified — the plan does not say which owner's exit code (if any) should now reflect discrepancies, or that reconcile-check had no such signal to preserve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9f57c8a89b3842f4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section + AC